# QA Bug Report (Awesome-adapted)

Use only when the user asks for a bug report, QA write-up, or reproduction doc. Does not replace Scout/Architect/Builder/QA workflow steps.

## Severity
1. **Critical** — crash, data loss, security, blocks all users
2. **High** — major feature broken / blocks many users
3. **Medium** — non-critical break / usability impact for some
4. **Low** — minor UI / typos / non-core
5. **Trivial** — cosmetic, minimal impact

## Structure
```
# Bug Report: [concise title]

## Description
[impact]

## Environment
- Device / OS / Browser
- Screen (if relevant)
- User role (if relevant) — no secrets/PII dumps

## Severity
[level] — [why]

## Steps to Reproduce
1. …
2. …

## Expected Behavior
…

## Actual Behavior
…

## Visual Evidence
[paths / descriptions — no credential screenshots]

## Console/Error Logs
[sanitize tokens/PII]

## Additional Notes
…

## Possible Fix
[optional, evidence-based]
```

## Practices
- One issue per report; factual; numbered steps; exact errors
- No blame language; no production secrets in reports (see `security-appsec`)
